.policy "sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation" revision 1
.description "Pass values to SQLAlchemy's text() as bound parameters, and quote or allow-list identifiers, instead of splicing them into the SQL string."
.language python
.mode log
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. SQLAlchemy's `text(...)` (resolved through imports: `from sqlalchemy import text`,
// `sa.text`, `from sqlalchemy import text as sql_text`, sqlmodel's re-export; lib/sqlalchemy's sa_text_call) and a
// connection's `exec_driver_sql(...)`, whose SQL string is built from a value that is not a constant: an f-string
// interpolation, `"…" % value`, `"…".format(value)`, `"…".replace(…, value)`, `sep.join(values)` or `a + b`. The SQL
// argument and each spliced value are followed to where they come from: the names the scope binds them to before the
// read or in the same loop (`sql = f"…"; sql += f"…"; text(sql)`, a loop variable to its iterable, `a, b = x, y` item by
// item, a module-level name to its value, an imported module variable to its value in its own module),
// `self.x`/`cls.x` to what the class or a base of the run assigns, a call of a function of the run to what it returns,
// and a parameter to its default and to the arguments the run's calls pass (the calling call's only, when the value
// was reached through that call's return, one level deep). A value is not a constant when one of those ends in
// something else: a parameter no call of the run passes (a route's, a public helper's), an attribute, a call outside
// the run, a subscript of a request. Reported at the call, naming the spliced expression.
//   session.execute(text(f"SELECT * FROM recipe WHERE name = '{name}'"))       reported
//   select(Recipe).order_by(text(f"{col} {direction}"))                          reported: col is a parameter
//   conn.exec_driver_sql(f"VACUUM ANALYZE {table}")                              reported
//   text(f'SELECT count(*) FROM "{self._collection_name}"')                      reported: an identifier
//   text("SELECT * FROM recipe WHERE name = :name").bindparams(name=name)        not reported: a bound parameter
//   text(f"SELECT * FROM {RECIPE_TABLE} LIMIT {int(limit)}")                     not reported: constants and a cast
// Constants it leaves alone: literals; values that end only in literals by the paths above (`direction = "DESC" if
// desc else "ASC"`, `for t in ("a", "b")`, `SORTS[key]` with SORTS a dict of literals, `match_sql("chat", key)` for
// `def match_sql(table, key)`, `cls._threshold` with `_threshold: ClassVar[float] = 0.5`, `sorted(Status.billable())`
// returning enum members); `int()`, `float()`, `len()`, `bool()` results; parameters annotated int, float, bool,
// Decimal or an enum of the run; an enum's own `self.value`; `M.__tablename__`; SQL rendered by SQLAlchemy
// (`str(expr.compile(...))`); bind-parameter names, an interpolation right after `:` in the literal
// (`f"… = :{param}"`, `', '.join(f':id_{i}' for i in range(n))`).
// Vetted values it leaves alone: a name its scope binds to a quoting call (`table = preparer.quote(table)`,
// `quote_identifier(...)`) or to a number cast of itself (`limit = int(limit)`), tests against an allow-list
// (`if col not in ("name", "created_at"): raise`) or checks in an `if`/`assert` with `re.fullmatch(…, x)` or
// `x.isidentifier()`; for an imported module variable, the same in its own module (`if METHOD not in (...):
// METHOD = ""`). Also left alone: a SQL string the function receives and passes on unchanged (`text(query)` with
// query a parameter: nothing is built here); other libraries' `text` (tagflow's and htpy's, a local `def text`);
// tests, Alembic revisions and files importing alembic (lib/sqlalchemy's sa_migration_doc; the alembic pack owns
// migrations) and hand-written migration modules (`migrations.py`, a `migrations/` directory), whose DDL splices
// table, index and sequence names read from the schema.
// Overlap: Ruff S608 / Bandit B608 match SQL keywords in any formatted string (`SELECT … FROM`, `UPDATE … SET`), so they
// miss fragments given to text() (`order_by(text(f"{col} {direction}"))`, `where(text(f"name = '{x}'"))`), flag
// constants and non-SQL strings, and are not ported in the `python` pack. python-security-sql-injection reports request
// data reaching SQL through the call graph; this rule reports the construct whatever the value's source.
// Gaps: the scope is taken as a whole (a name quoted or allow-listed anywhere in its scope counts as vetted at every
// read); a helper whose callers the call graph resolves only in part is judged by those callers; an identifier read
// from the schema or the model's metadata (`column.name`, `self.table.name`) is reported; SQL built in another
// function and passed in as a parameter is not followed; `session.execute("…")` with a plain string (SQLAlchemy 1.x) is
// not a sink.

#include "lib/sqlalchemy.rerail"

.violation TextInterpolation(at: node, fn: symbol, what: symbol) "The SQL given to `{fn}()` splices in {what}: pass values as bound parameters (`:name` in the SQL, with `.bindparams(name=...)` or the execute parameters dict), and quote identifiers (table, column) with the dialect's identifier preparer or pick them from a fixed allow-list. Leave it only when the value is already one of those."
TextInterpolation(c, fn, what) :- sqt_sink(c, fn, _), a = min a2 : { sqt_named(c, a2) }, sqt_what(a, what).
// sqt_named(c, a): a is spliced straight into sink c's SQL (an interpolated expression, an operand of `+`/`%`, a
// format() argument) and carries a value that is not a constant: the piece the message names.
.decl sqt_named(c: node, a: node)
sqt_named(c, a) :- sqt_piece(c, e, k), sqt_edge(c, e, k, a, k2, 1), sqt_var_under(c, a, k2).
// sqt_what(a, what): the spliced expression, quoted when it fits on one short line.
.decl sqt_what(a: node, what: symbol)
sqt_what(a, what) :- sqt_named(_, a), text(a, t), match("[^\n]{1,60}", t), what = @replace_all(t, "^(.*)$", "`$1`").
sqt_what(a, "a value that is not a constant") :- sqt_named(_, a), text(a, t), !match("[^\n]{1,60}", t).

// ---- sinks -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// sqt_sink(c, fn, v): call c runs SQL text v: SQLAlchemy's `text(v)` (or `text(text=v)`), `<conn>.exec_driver_sql(v)`
// in a file importing SQLAlchemy; not in test code, an Alembic revision or a hand-written migration module.
.decl sqt_sink(c: node, fn: symbol, v: node)
sqt_sink(c, "text", v) :- sa_text_call(c), sqt_sql_arg(c, "text", v0), unparen(v0, v), docof(c, d), !sqt_skipped_doc(d).
sqt_sink(c, "exec_driver_sql", v) :- call_name(c, "exec_driver_sql"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, _),
    sqt_sql_arg(c, "statement", v0), unparen(v0, v), docof(c, d), sa_doc(d), !sqt_skipped_doc(d).
.decl sqt_sql_arg(c: node, k: symbol, v: node)
sqt_sql_arg(c, k, v) :- kind(c, "call"), (k = "text" ; k = "statement"), posarg(c, 0, v).
sqt_sql_arg(c, k, v) :- kind(c, "call"), (k = "text" ; k = "statement"), call_arg(c, -1, k, v).
// sqt_skipped_doc(d): test code, an Alembic revision, or a hand-written schema migration module (`migrations.py`,
// `migrate_*.py`, a `migrations/` directory), whose DDL splices table, index and sequence names read from the schema.
.decl sqt_skipped_doc(d: number)
sqt_skipped_doc(d) :- sa_test_doc(d).
sqt_skipped_doc(d) :- sa_migration_doc(d).
sqt_skipped_doc(d) :- file_name(d, s), (s = "migrations.py" ; s = "migration.py" ; s = "migrate.py" ;
    glob("migrate_*.py", s)).
sqt_skipped_doc(d) :- doc(d, _, _), (path_part(d, "migrations") ; path_part(d, "migration")).

// ---- pieces: what the SQL text is made of ------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Each piece is reached in a context k: the call whose return value it was reached through (one level deep), or the
// sink c itself when there is none. A parameter read in context k, a call of its function, is the argument that call
// passes; read without one, it is every argument the run's calls pass. So a helper called with a literal here and a
// variable elsewhere is judged at each call.
// sqt_piece(c, p, k): p is a value the SQL text of sink c is made of, reached from the argument through names,
// parentheses, conditionals and calls only; sqt_spliced(c, p, k): reached through a build on the way (an
// interpolation, `%`, `+`, format(), replace(), join()).
.decl sqt_piece(c: node, p: node, k: node)
sqt_piece(c, v, c) :- sqt_sink(c, _, v).
sqt_piece(c, a, k2) :- sqt_piece(c, e, k), sqt_edge(c, e, k, a, k2, 0).
.decl sqt_spliced(c: node, p: node, k: node)
sqt_spliced(c, a, k2) :- sqt_piece(c, e, k), sqt_edge(c, e, k, a, k2, 1).
sqt_spliced(c, a, k2) :- sqt_spliced(c, e, k), sqt_edge(c, e, k, a, k2, _).
.decl sqt_seen(c: node, e: node, k: node)
sqt_seen(c, e, k) :- sqt_piece(c, e, k).
sqt_seen(c, e, k) :- sqt_spliced(c, e, k).
// sqt_edge(c, e, k, a, k2, s): piece e of sink c, in context k, is made of a, in context k2; s is 1 for a build.
.decl sqt_edge(c: node, e: node, k: node, a: node, k2: node, s: number)
sqt_edge(c, e, k, a, k, s) :- sqt_seen(c, e, k), sqt_step(e, a, s).
// A call of a function of the run: what it returns, in the call's context.
sqt_edge(c, e, k, v, e, 0) :- sqt_seen(c, e, k), sqt_ret(e, v).
// A parameter: its default, and the argument the context's call passes, or with no such context every call's. A
// parameter annotated as a number or an enum, or vetted, is a constant leaf instead.
sqt_edge(c, r, k, v, k, 0) :- sqt_seen(c, r, k), sqt_param_flows(r, g, x), sqt_param_default(g, x, v).
sqt_edge(c, r, k, v, c, 0) :- sqt_seen(c, r, k), sqt_param_flows(r, g, x), sqt_param_at(k, g, v, x).
sqt_edge(c, r, k, v, c, 0) :- sqt_seen(c, r, k), sqt_param_flows(r, g, x), !sqt_target(k, g), sqt_param_at(_, g, v, x).
.decl sqt_param_flows(r: node, g: node, x: symbol)
sqt_param_flows(r, g, x) :- sqt_param_ref(r, g, x), !sqt_trusted_name(r), !sqt_typed_param(g, x).
// sqt_var(c, p, k): sink c's SQL text is built from p, a value that is not a constant: a leaf piece that is no
// constant, or a parameter no call passes in its context (a route's, a public helper's), not annotated as a number or
// an enum and not vetted.
.decl sqt_var(c: node, p: node, k: node)
sqt_var(c, p, k) :- sqt_spliced(c, p, k), !sqt_edge(c, p, k, _, _, _), !sqt_const_leaf(p).
sqt_var(c, p, k) :- sqt_spliced(c, p, k), sqt_param_ref(p, g, x), !sqt_target(k, g), !sqt_passed(g, x),
    !sqt_typed_param(g, x), !sqt_trusted_name(p).
// sqt_var_under(c, a, k): spliced piece a of sink c, in context k, is, or is made of, a value sqt_var reports.
.decl sqt_var_under(c: node, a: node, k: node)
sqt_var_under(c, p, k) :- sqt_var(c, p, k).
sqt_var_under(c, e, k) :- sqt_spliced(c, e, k), sqt_edge(c, e, k, a, k2, _), sqt_var_under(c, a, k2).

// sqt_step(e, a, s): e's value is made of a's; s is 1 when the step splices a into a string.
.decl sqt_step(e: node, a: node, s: number)
sqt_step(p, a, 0) :- kind(p, "parenthesized_expression"), unparen(p, a), p != a.
sqt_step(w, a, 0) :- kind(w, "await"), child(w, a, 0).
sqt_step(s, a, 1) :- kind(s, "string"), child(s, i, _), kind(i, "interpolation"), !sqt_bind_name(i),
    field(i, "expression", a).
sqt_step(s, a, 0) :- kind(s, "concatenated_string"), child(s, a, _), kind(a, "string").
sqt_step(b, a, 0) :- kind(b, "boolean_operator"), (field(b, "left", a) ; field(b, "right", a)).
sqt_step(b, a, 1) :- kind(b, "binary_operator"), op(b, o), (o = "+" ; o = "%"), (field(b, "left", a) ; field(b, "right", a)).
sqt_step(c, a, 0) :- kind(c, "conditional_expression"), (child(c, a, 0) ; child(c, a, 2)).
sqt_step(t, a, 0) :- (kind(t, "tuple") ; kind(t, "list") ; kind(t, "set") ; kind(t, "expression_list")), child(t, a, _),
    !kind(a, "comment").
sqt_step(t, a, 0) :- kind(t, "dictionary"), child(t, p, _), kind(p, "pair"), field(p, "value", a).
sqt_step(t, a, 0) :- (kind(t, "list_comprehension") ; kind(t, "generator_expression") ; kind(t, "set_comprehension")),
    field(t, "body", a).
// `"…".format(x)`, `sql.replace("{t}", t)`, `", ".join(cols)`: the receiver as is, the arguments spliced (a quoting
// `replace` is a constant leaf instead).
sqt_step(c, r, 0) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, r, m), sqt_build_method(m), !sqt_sanitizer(c).
sqt_step(c, a, 1) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, m), sqt_build_method(m), !sqt_sanitizer(c),
    call_arg(c, _, _, a).
sqt_step(c, a, 1) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, m), sqt_build_method(m), !sqt_sanitizer(c),
    field(c, "arguments", al), child(al, sp, _), (kind(sp, "list_splat") ; kind(sp, "dictionary_splat")), child(sp, a, 0).
sqt_step(c, g, 1) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, "join"), field(c, "arguments", g),
    kind(g, "generator_expression").
// `str(x)` is x; `sorted(xs)`, `list(xs)`, `tuple(xs)`, `set(xs)`, `frozenset(xs)`, `reversed(xs)` hold xs's items.
sqt_step(c, a, 0) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), sym_of(f, q), (q = "builtins.str" ; q = "builtins.sorted" ;
    q = "builtins.list" ; q = "builtins.tuple" ; q = "builtins.set" ; q = "builtins.frozenset" ;
    q = "builtins.reversed"), posarg(c, 0, a).
// `M[k]` and `M.get(k, d)` are one of M's values (or d): `SORTS[key]` with `SORTS = {"new": "created_at DESC"}`.
sqt_step(x, o, 0) :- kind(x, "subscript"), field(x, "value", o).
sqt_step(c, o, 0) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, "get").
sqt_step(c, d, 0) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, "get"), posarg(c, 1, d).
// sqt_ret(c, v): call c of a function of the run returns v (a quoting call is a constant leaf instead).
.decl sqt_ret(c: node, v: node)
sqt_ret(c, v) :- kind(c, "call"), !sqt_sanitizer(c), sqt_target(c, g), kind(r, "return_statement"), child(r, v, 0),
    nearest(r, g, fdef).
// A name: what the scope that binds it binds it to (the function, a comprehension, the module) at a binding that can
// reach the read; an imported module variable's value in its own module (parameters: sqt_edge). Not a name the scope
// quotes or checks against an allow-list (sqt_trusted_name).
sqt_step(r, v, 0) :- kind(r, "identifier"), !sqt_trusted_name(r), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), sqt_bind(h, x, v, s),
    r != v, (nearest(r, h2, fscope), h2 != h ; kind(h, k), comp_scope(k) ; earlier(s, r) ;
    (kind(l, "for_statement") ; kind(l, "while_statement")), within(s, l), within(r, l)).
sqt_step(r, v, 0) :- (kind(r, "identifier") ; kind(r, "attribute")), !sqt_trusted_name(r), sym_of(r, q),
    sa_module_var(q, v).
// `self.x` / `cls.x`: what the class or a base of the run assigns it, in its body (`x: ClassVar[float] = 0.5`) or
// as `self.x = v` / `cls.x = v` in a method.
sqt_step(p, v, 0) :- sqt_self_attr(p, _, a), sqt_class_up(p, b), sa_class_attr(b, a, v, _).
sqt_step(p, v, 0) :- sqt_self_attr(p, _, a), sqt_class_up(p, b), kind(s, "assignment"), field(s, "left", l),
    attr_of(l, o, a), kind(o, "identifier"), (text(o, "self") ; text(o, "cls")), within(s, b), field(s, "right", v).
.decl sqt_build_method(m: symbol)
sqt_build_method("format"). sqt_build_method("format_map"). sqt_build_method("join"). sqt_build_method("replace").

// sqt_bind(h, x, v, s): scope h binds name x to a value made of v's at s: `x = v`, `x: T = v`, `x += v`, `x := v`,
// `a, x = u, v` (item by item, through parentheses and conditionals), `a, x = v`, `for x in v` (a statement or a
// comprehension clause).
.decl sqt_bind(h: node, x: symbol, v: node, s: node)
sqt_bind(h, x, v, a) :- asg(h, x, v, a).
sqt_bind(h, x, v, a) :- kind(a, "augmented_assignment"), field(a, "left", l), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, x),
    field(a, "right", v), nearest(a, h, scope).
sqt_bind(h, x, v, a) :- kind(a, "named_expression"), field(a, "name", l), text(l, x), field(a, "value", v),
    nearest(a, h, fscope).
sqt_bind(h, x, v, a) :- kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), (kind(l, "pattern_list") ; kind(l, "tuple_pattern")),
    child(l, i, k), kind(i, "identifier"), text(i, x), field(a, "right", r), sqt_unpack(r, k, v), nearest(a, h, scope).
sqt_bind(h, x, r, a) :- kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), (kind(l, "pattern_list") ; kind(l, "tuple_pattern")),
    child(l, i, _), kind(i, "identifier"), text(i, x), field(a, "right", r), !sqt_unpackable(r), nearest(a, h, scope).
sqt_bind(h, x, v, s) :- kind(s, "for_statement"), field(s, "left", l), sqt_target_name(l, x), field(s, "right", v),
    nearest(s, h, scope).
sqt_bind(h, x, v, s) :- kind(s, "for_in_clause"), field(s, "left", l), sqt_target_name(l, x), field(s, "right", v),
    nearest(s, h, comp_scope).
// The binding s must be able to reach the read r: r is in a function nested in h (it runs later), h is a
// comprehension, s comes before r, or s and r share a loop (a read early in a loop body sees a binding later in it).
// `for chat_id, author_id in rows:` after the text() call does not feed the author_id the SQL was built from.
.decl sqt_target_name(l: node, x: symbol)
sqt_target_name(l, x) :- kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, x).
sqt_target_name(l, x) :- (kind(l, "pattern_list") ; kind(l, "tuple_pattern")), child(l, i, _), kind(i, "identifier"),
    text(i, x).
// sqt_unpack(r, k, v): item k of the tuple r spells out, through parentheses, conditional branches, `await` and the
// returns of a function of the run (`method, options = self._index_config()` with `return method, options`).
.decl sqt_unpack(r: node, k: number, v: node)
sqt_unpack(r, k, v) :- (kind(r, "expression_list") ; kind(r, "tuple")), !has(r, _, "comment"),
    count : { child(r, sp, _), kind(sp, "list_splat") } = 0, child(r, v, k).
sqt_unpack(p, k, v) :- kind(p, "parenthesized_expression"), unparen(p, r), p != r, sqt_unpack(r, k, v).
sqt_unpack(c, k, v) :- kind(c, "conditional_expression"), (child(c, b, 0) ; child(c, b, 2)), sqt_unpack(b, k, v).
sqt_unpack(w, k, v) :- kind(w, "await"), child(w, c, 0), sqt_unpack(c, k, v).
sqt_unpack(c, k, v) :- kind(c, "call"), sqt_target(c, g), kind(r, "return_statement"), nearest(r, g, fdef),
    child(r, t, 0), sqt_unpack(t, k, v).
.decl sqt_unpackable(r: node)
sqt_unpackable(r) :- sqt_unpack(r, _, _).

// ---- parameters and attributes -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// sqt_param_ref(r, g, x): name r reads parameter x of function g.
.decl sqt_param_ref(r: node, g: node, x: symbol)
sqt_param_ref(r, g, x) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, g), param(g, x, _).
// sqt_target(c, g): call c calls function g of the run: the call graph's target, or a def nested in the calling
// function by name (`def author(path): …` then `author("$.user_id")`).
.decl sqt_target(c: node, g: node)
sqt_target(c, g) :- call_target(c, g).
sqt_target(c, g) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), kind(f, "identifier"), text(f, x), look(f, x, h),
    kind(h, "function_definition"), defn(h, x, g).
// sqt_param_at(c, g, a, x): call c passes argument a to g's parameter x (lib/security's sec_param_at).
.decl sqt_param_at(c: node, g: node, a: node, x: symbol)
sqt_param_at(c, g, a, x) :- sqt_target(c, g), posarg(c, i, a), !sqt_bound_method(c, g), param(g, x, i).
sqt_param_at(c, g, a, x) :- sqt_bound_method(c, g), posarg(c, i, a), j = i + 1, param(g, x, j).
sqt_param_at(c, g, a, x) :- sqt_target(c, g), call_arg(c, -1, x, a), param(g, x, _).
// sqt_bound_method(c, g): c calls method g through an instance or its class (`obj.m(a)`, `C(a)` for `__init__`):
// the first parameter is self.
.decl sqt_bound_method(c: node, g: node)
sqt_bound_method(c, g) :- call_target(c, g), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, _), nearest(g, k, scope),
    kind(k, "class_definition"), !sqt_static(g).
sqt_bound_method(c, g) :- call_target(c, g), def_name(g, "__init__"), field(c, "function", f), !attr_of(f, _, _).
.decl sqt_static(g: node)
sqt_static(g) :- decorator(g, e), text(e, "staticmethod").
// sqt_passed(g, x): some call of the run passes g's parameter x.
.decl sqt_passed(g: node, x: symbol)
sqt_passed(g, x) :- sqt_param_at(_, g, _, x).
.decl sqt_param_default(g: node, x: symbol, v: node)
sqt_param_default(g, x, v) :- field(g, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, _),
    (kind(p, "default_parameter") ; kind(p, "typed_default_parameter")), field(p, "name", n), text(n, x),
    field(p, "value", v).
// sqt_self_attr(p, c, a): p is `self.a` or `cls.a` in a method of class c.
.decl sqt_self_attr(p: node, c: node, a: symbol)
sqt_self_attr(p, c, a) :- attr_of(p, o, a), kind(o, "identifier"), (text(o, "self") ; text(o, "cls")),
    nearest(p, c, sqt_class_kind).
.decl sqt_class_kind(k: symbol)
sqt_class_kind("class_definition").
// sqt_class_up(p, b): b is the class of `self.a` read p, or one of its bases of the run.
.decl sqt_class_up(p: node, b: node)
sqt_class_up(p, c) :- sqt_self_attr(p, c, _).
sqt_class_up(p, b) :- sqt_class_up(p, c), class_base(c, q), class_def(b, q).

// ---- constants ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// sqt_const_leaf(p): a piece that cannot carry outside text: a literal (a string whose only interpolations are bind
// parameter names among them), a number, True/False/None, a negative number, an int()/float()/len()/bool() result,
// a model's `__tablename__`, SQL a SQLAlchemy construct renders (`stmt.compile(...)`, literals escaped by the
// dialect), a parameter annotated as a number or an enum, an enum's own `self.value`/`self.name`, a quoting call or a
// vetted name.
.decl sqt_const_leaf(p: node)
sqt_const_leaf(p) :- ast_constant(p).
sqt_const_leaf(p) :- kind(p, "string").
sqt_const_leaf(p) :- kind(p, "unary_operator"), field(p, "argument", a), (kind(a, "integer") ; kind(a, "float")).
sqt_const_leaf(p) :- kind(p, "call"), field(p, "function", f), sym_of(f, q), (q = "builtins.int" ; q = "builtins.float" ;
    q = "builtins.len" ; q = "builtins.bool").
sqt_const_leaf(p) :- attr_of(p, _, "__tablename__").
sqt_const_leaf(p) :- call_name(p, "compile"), field(p, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, _).
sqt_const_leaf(p) :- sqt_param_ref(p, g, x), sqt_typed_param(g, x).
sqt_const_leaf(p) :- sqt_self_attr(p, c, a), (a = "value" ; a = "name"), class_def(c, q), sqt_enum_q(q).
sqt_const_leaf(p) :- sqt_sanitizer(p).
sqt_const_leaf(p) :- sqt_trusted_name(p).
// sqt_typed_param(f, x): function f's parameter x is annotated int, float, bool or Decimal (or Optional of one),
// `order_id: int | None = None`, or an enum class of the run, `event: WebhookEventType`.
.decl sqt_typed_param(f: node, x: symbol)
sqt_typed_param(f, x) :- field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, _), sqt_param_name(p, x), field(p, "type", t),
    text(t, tt), match("(int|float|bool|Decimal)( *\\| *None)?|(Optional|typing\\.Optional)\\[(int|float|bool|Decimal)\\]", tt).
sqt_typed_param(f, x) :- field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, _), sqt_param_name(p, x), field(p, "type", t),
    child(t, e, 0), sym_of(e, q), sqt_enum_q(q).
// sqt_enum_q(q): q is a class of the run deriving from enum.Enum (StrEnum, IntEnum, Flag), through the run's classes.
.decl sqt_enum_q(q: symbol)
sqt_enum_q(q) :- class_def(c, q), class_base(c, b), (b = "enum.Enum" ; b = "enum.StrEnum" ; b = "enum.IntEnum" ;
    b = "enum.Flag" ; b = "enum.IntFlag").
sqt_enum_q(q) :- class_def(c, q), class_base(c, b), sqt_enum_q(b).
.decl sqt_param_name(p: node, x: symbol)
sqt_param_name(p, x) :- kind(p, "typed_parameter"), child(p, n, 0), kind(n, "identifier"), text(n, x).
sqt_param_name(p, x) :- kind(p, "typed_default_parameter"), field(p, "name", n), text(n, x).
// sqt_sanitizer(c): c quotes an identifier: `preparer.quote(name)`, `quote_identifier(name)`, `cls.quote_table(t, d)`,
// `format_table(t)`, or doubles the quote character the way a quoted identifier or literal escapes it
// (`name.replace('"', '""')`, `value.replace("'", "''")`).
.decl sqt_sanitizer(c: node)
sqt_sanitizer(c) :- kind(c, "call"), call_name(c, m),
    match("quote(_[a-z]+)*|format_table|format_column|escape_identifier|escape_ident", m).
sqt_sanitizer(c) :- kind(c, "call"), call_name(c, "replace"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, _), posarg(c, 0, a),
    posarg(c, 1, b), str(a, q), str(b, qq), (q = "\"", qq = "\"\"" ; q = "'", qq = "''" ; q = "`", qq = "``").
// sqt_trusted_name(r): name r is one its scope vets: bound there to a quoting call (`table, column = quote(table),
// quote(column)`) or to a number cast of itself (`limit = int(limit)`), tested there against an allow-list
// (`if col not in ("name", "created_at"): raise …`), or checked in an `if`/`assert` by a pattern or a str predicate
// (`if not re.fullmatch(r"[a-z_]+", key): raise …`, `assert name.isidentifier()`); for an imported module variable,
// the same in its module (`if METHOD not in ALLOWED: METHOD = ""`, `try: LISTS = int(LISTS)`). The scope is taken as
// a whole: a read before the vetting counts as vetted too.
.decl sqt_trusted_name(r: node)
sqt_trusted_name(r) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), sqt_vetted(h, x).
sqt_trusted_name(r) :- (kind(r, "identifier") ; kind(r, "attribute")), sym_of(r, q), sqt_module_vetted(q).
.decl sqt_vetted(h: node, x: symbol)
sqt_vetted(h, x) :- sqt_bind(h, x, v, _), unparen(v, c), sqt_sanitizer(c).
sqt_vetted(h, x) :- sqt_bind(h, x, v, _), unparen(v, c), kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), sym_of(f, q),
    (q = "builtins.int" ; q = "builtins.float"), posarg(c, 0, a), kind(a, "identifier"), text(a, x).
sqt_vetted(h, x) :- sqt_allowlisted(h, x).
sqt_vetted(h, x) :- sqt_check_call(c, x), sqt_in_test(c), nearest(c, h, scope).
// sqt_in_test(c): c is (in) the condition of an `if`/`elif` or the test of an `assert`.
.decl sqt_in_test(c: node)
sqt_in_test(c) :- (kind(i, "if_statement") ; kind(i, "elif_clause")), field(i, "condition", t), (c = t ; within(c, t)),
    kind(c, "call").
sqt_in_test(c) :- kind(i, "assert_statement"), child(i, t, 0), (c = t ; within(c, t)), kind(c, "call").
// sqt_check_call(c, x): call c checks name x's text: `re.fullmatch(p, x)` / `re.match(p, x)`, `PATTERN.fullmatch(x)`,
// `x.isidentifier()`, `x.isalnum()`, `x.isdigit()`.
.decl sqt_check_call(c: node, x: symbol)
sqt_check_call(c, x) :- call_name(c, m), (m = "fullmatch" ; m = "match"), call_arg(c, _, _, a), kind(a, "identifier"),
    text(a, x).
sqt_check_call(c, x) :- call_name(c, m), (m = "isidentifier" ; m = "isalnum" ; m = "isdigit" ; m = "isdecimal"),
    field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, _), kind(o, "identifier"), text(o, x).
.decl sqt_module_vetted(q: symbol)
sqt_module_vetted(q) :- sqt_vetted(m, x), kind(m, "module"), modname(m, mq), q = @dot(mq, x).
// sqt_allowlisted(h, x): scope h tests `x in S` or `x not in S`, S a collection of literals or an UPPER_CASE name.
.decl sqt_allowlisted(h: node, x: symbol)
sqt_allowlisted(h, x) :- cmp(c, op, l, r), (op = "in" ; op = "not in"), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, x),
    sqt_allow_set(r), nearest(c, h, scope).
.decl sqt_allow_set(r: node)
sqt_allow_set(r) :- unparen(r, t), (kind(t, "tuple") ; kind(t, "list") ; kind(t, "set")),
    count : { child(t, i, _), !kind(i, "comment"), !ast_constant(i) } = 0.
sqt_allow_set(r) :- unparen(r, n), leaf_name(n, x), match("_?[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*", x).
// sqt_bind_name(i): interpolation i names a bind parameter: the literal right before it ends in `:` and a name's
// start (`= :{param}`, `:p_{i}`), not in a `::` cast.
.decl sqt_bind_name(i: node)
sqt_bind_name(i) :- kind(i, "interpolation"), child(s, i, k), j = k - 1, child(s, p, j), kind(p, "string_content"),
    text(p, t), match("(?s)(.*[^:])?:[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9]*|(?s)(.*[^:])?:", t).

// The cases, `cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/`, read as one repository: each line ending in `# caught`
// is reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "app/__init__.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/app/__init__.py"
    .fixture "app/config.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/app/config.py"
    .fixture "app/enums.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/app/enums.py"
    .fixture "app/migrations.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/app/migrations.py"
    .fixture "app/models.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/app/models.py"
    .fixture "app/repo.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/app/repo.py"
    .fixture "app/search.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/app/search.py"
    .fixture "migrations/versions/0002_backfill.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/migrations/versions/0002_backfill.py"
    .fixture "tests/__init__.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/tests/__init__.py"
    .fixture "tests/test_repo.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/tests/test_repo.py"
    .fixture "ui/__init__.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/ui/__init__.py"
    .fixture "ui/components.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/ui/components.py"
    .fixture "ui/local_text.py" from "../cases/sqlalchemy-practice-text-interpolation/ui/local_text.py"
    .expect _ at "app/enums.py":24
    .expect _ at "app/enums.py":71
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":13
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":17
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":22
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":26
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":30
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":34
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":39
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":48
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":53
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":57
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":62
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":71
    .expect _ at "app/repo.py":77
    .expect _ at "app/search.py":23
    .expect _ at "app/search.py":27
